# Implementation kit: Cascade Sleep & Respiratory

*Fictional customer. Every number marked **(A)** is an assumption to replace in discovery;
every number marked **(M)** is measured on this repo's synthetic eval (`make eval`,
{{EVAL_DATE}}).*

---

## 1. Discovery and operational audit

**Who they are (A).** Regional sleep and respiratory DME supplier, Washington and Oregon.
~1,500 new PAP orders a month, growing into home oxygen. Six intake coordinators. Orders
arrive by fax from ~400 referring practices; billing runs in Brightree.

**Current intake workflow (A).**

```
fax line ─► shared inbox ─► coordinator opens packet ─► keys order into Brightree
                                  │
                                  ├─ checks: signed order? F2F before sleep test?
                                  │  AHI and events? MBI? NPI? eligibility portal
                                  │
                complete ◄────────┴────────► incomplete: call or fax the office,
                   │                         park it, re-check when papers return
                   ▼
             schedule setup
```

**Where the time goes (A).** ~18 minutes of hands-on time per order: 4 min finding and
ordering pages, 5 min keying, 6 min checking criteria, 3 min eligibility lookup. Incomplete
orders add a 10-minute outreach cycle, usually more than once.

**Top defect types.** The synthetic set plants the defects that drive Medicare PAP
documentation errors in published DME MAC review findings: missing or unsigned orders,
face-to-face notes that don't predate the sleep test, AHI 5–14 without a documented
qualifying condition, missing sleep study pages, and provider or eligibility problems.
In discovery, replace the planted mix with 200 of their own recent orders, labeled by a
senior coordinator.

| Defect (planted) | Share of synthetic orders | Who fixes it |
|---|---|---|
| Unsigned order | {{UNSIGNED}} | Referring office (needs info) |
| F2F after sleep test | {{F2F}} | Referring office (needs info) |
| Sleep study page missing | {{MISSING_STUDY}} | Referring office (needs info) |
| AHI 5–14, no qualifying condition documented | {{MILD}} | Reviewer, then office |
| Invalid / inactive NPI | {{NPI}} | Reviewer |
| Eligibility inactive | {{ELIG}} | Reviewer / billing |
| Key field illegible | {{ILLEGIBLE}} | Reviewer |

